==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{ety|ru|id=picture|:bor|it:cartina|tree=1}}
{{bor+|ru|it|cartina|t=fine paper}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|карти́на}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-картина.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|карти́на|adj=карти́нный|dim=карти́нка}}

# [[picture]] (representation of visible reality produced by drawing, etc.)
# [[painting]], [[canvas]]
# [[movie]], [[film]]
#: {{syn|ru|фильм|кинофи́льм|кинокарти́на|ле́нта|киноле́нта}}
# [[picture]], [[image]] (as produced in transient fashion by technology, e.g. a monitor)
# [[scene]]

====Usage notes====
For sense 1, this term is often used in the sense of referring to a painting created by hand and perceived as a work of art. On the other hand, ''[[картинка]]'' is preferably used for photographs and other non-transient images created with the help of technology.

